What Challenges Affect the Pressure Sensors Market?

Price competition, calibration requirements, long-term stability and application-specific certification influence the market. Sensors used in demanding environments must resist temperature changes, vibration, contamination and chemical exposure.

Manufacturers must also balance sensitivity, power consumption, packaging size and production cost. Integration with connected monitoring systems can create opportunities, but it also increases requirements for electronics, communication interfaces and data reliability.

